comments.body:
@RONNCC I reproduced the reference loss on macOS with Herdr 0.9.3 and OMP 18.2.4: sending SIGTERM to OMP while leaving Herdr running causes process-exit handling to clear the native session reference, so the next autosave keeps only the shell even though the JSONL file still exists.

The fix is in https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr/pull/5081. Pi/OMP shutdown hooks now confirm the selected session and report TERM/HUP interruption within a bounded deadline. Herdr keeps that recovery reference separately from live agent state. I verified interrupted-session restoration with OMP 18.2.4 and Pi 1.1.0, including Pi with OSC 7501 enabled; normal interactive quit still clears the reference. Regression tests also cover switching sessions while an older state request is stalled. This is graceful-shutdown recovery, so a hard kill that cannot run the native shutdown hook remains outside this path.

All CI checks on the latest commit dae8a818 are green, including macOS, Linux, Windows and Windows ConPTY. CodeRabbit and Greptile have completed their latest reviews with no outstanding actionable findings. The PR is ready for maintainer review/merge; the fix is not yet included in the released 0.9.3 binary.
